---
import Header from "@components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "@components/Footer.astro";
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
import Main from "@layouts/Main.astro";

const emailHref = "mailto:nivoset@gmail.com?subject=Automation%20pain%20point";
---

<Layout
  title="Automation Help | Nivoset"
  description="Practical AI and automation help for local companies that need to make messy work visible without hiring someone full time."
>
  <Header activeNav="automation" />
  <Main
    pageTitle="Automation help for messy work"
    pageDesc="I help local companies turn spreadsheets, order forms, tracking sheets, reporting pain points, and repeated admin work into practical systems without hiring someone full time."
  >
    <section class="intro-panel" aria-labelledby="intro-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">Practical automation</p>
        <h2 id="intro-heading">
          Recover wasted hours without turning it into a software project.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Most useful automation starts with a familiar pain point: an Excel
          sheet that has become the source of truth, an order form that starts a
          messy chain of follow-ups, or a weekly report that takes too much
          manual cleanup before anyone can trust it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a class="primary-cta" href={emailHref}>Send me your pain points</a>
    </section>

    <section class="problem-grid" aria-label="Automation capabilities">
      <article>
        <p class="section-kicker">Spreadsheets</p>
        <h2>Excel and reporting cleanup</h2>
        <p>
          Turn recurring spreadsheet work into repeatable flows that clean,
          check, summarize, and surface what changed.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <p class="section-kicker">Intake</p>
        <h2>Forms, email, and handoffs</h2>
        <p>
          Convert scattered order forms, inbox requests, and notes into a clearer
          workflow with ownership and next steps.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <p class="section-kicker">Tracking</p>
        <h2>Work and order status</h2>
        <p>
          Make it easier to see where jobs, orders, or requests are stuck, who
          owns them, and what needs attention.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <p class="section-kicker">Tools</p>
        <h2>Small internal systems</h2>
        <p>
          Build simple tools around the way your business actually works, then
          document them so your team can keep using them.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="automation-section" aria-labelledby="proof-heading">
      <p class="section-kicker">What this can look like</p>
      <h2 id="proof-heading">A few practical examples</h2>
      <div class="example-list">
        <article>
          <h3>Weekly reporting stops being detective work</h3>
          <p>
            A spreadsheet that used to require manual cleanup becomes a
            repeatable check-and-report flow, so exceptions stand out before
            people waste time reading every row.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>Follow-up work gets easier to review</h3>
          <p>
            Repeated customer or internal follow-ups can become draftable,
            trackable, and easier to approve, with AI used only where it saves
            time without removing judgment.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>Order status becomes visible</h3>
          <p>
            Instead of one fragile tracking sheet, a small internal tool can show
            what came in, what is waiting, who owns it, and what needs a decision.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class="automation-section split-section"
      aria-labelledby="fit-heading"
    >
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">Good fit</p>
        <h2 id="fit-heading">Work worth improving</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Recurring reports that take too long to prepare.</li>
          <li>Spreadsheets that track important work but are hard to trust.</li>
          <li>Order, job, or request status that is unclear until someone asks.</li>
          <li>Manual copy-and-paste between systems, forms, or inboxes.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">Not a fit</p>
        <h2>Work that wastes time</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Vague requests to add AI everywhere.</li>
          <li>Risky unsupervised automation where people still need judgment.</li>
          <li>Brittle hacks that nobody can understand or maintain later.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="automation-section" aria-labelledby="process-heading">
      <p class="section-kicker">How I work</p>
      <h2 id="process-heading">
        Translate messy work into systems people can use
      </h2>
      <p>
        I start by understanding the pain point, then look for the smallest
        useful change: a cleaner workflow, a repeatable report, a better tracking
        view, or a small internal tool. I care about confidential business data,
        customer lists, order details, and internal process information, so the
        shape of the solution should fit the risk of the work.
      </p>
      <p>
        When something is worth building, I document and teach enough that your
        team knows what exists and how to use it. Ongoing help is optional; the
        first goal is to make the next useful step clear.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-panel" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">Start small</p>
        <h2 id="cta-heading">Send me the pain points you have.</h2>
        <p>
          Reporting, tracking, understanding what is happening, or cleaning up a
          process that keeps stealing time are all good places to start. I will
          tell you whether it looks worth pursuing and what the smallest useful
          next step could be.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a class="primary-cta" href={emailHref}>Send me your pain points</a>
    </section>
  </Main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  @reference "tailwindcss";

  .intro-panel,
  .automation-section,
  .cta-panel {
    @apply rounded-md border border-gray-200/70 bg-white/70 p-6 shadow-sm dark:border-slate-800/70 dark:bg-slate-900/40;
  }

  .intro-panel,
  .cta-panel {
    @apply flex flex-col gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between;
  }

  .problem-grid {
    @apply mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2;
  }

  .problem-grid article {
    @apply rounded-md border border-gray-200/70 bg-white/70 p-6 shadow-sm dark:border-slate-800/70 dark:bg-slate-900/40;
  }

  .automation-section,
  .cta-panel {
    @apply mt-8;
  }

  .section-kicker {
    @apply text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400;
  }

  h2 {
    @apply text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100;
  }

  h3 {
    @apply text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100;
  }

  p,
  li {
    @apply leading-relaxed text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300;
  }

  ul {
    @apply mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5;
  }

  .intro-panel p,
  .automation-section p,
  .cta-panel p {
    @apply mt-4;
  }

  .example-list {
    @apply mt-5 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3;
  }

  .example-list article {
    @apply rounded-md border border-gray-200/70 p-4 dark:border-slate-800/70;
  }

  .example-list p {
    @apply text-sm;
  }

  .split-section {
    @apply grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2;
  }

  .primary-cta {
    @apply inline-flex w-fit shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-blue-600 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-sm transition-colors hover:bg-blue-700 focus-visible:no-underline dark:bg-blue-500 dark:text-slate-950 dark:hover:bg-blue-400;
  }
</style>
